# =============================================================================
# CardDemo Java (Maven / Spring Boot) — Docker build-context ignore rules
# =============================================================================
# Purpose (QA FINAL 7 F-3): keep build output, VCS metadata, local logs, secrets,
# and IDE/OS cruft OUT of the Docker build context — for context-transfer
# efficiency and defense-in-depth (so a stray local `.env` can never leak into an
# image layer). This mirrors the intent of .gitignore for the image build.
#
# IMPORTANT — do NOT exclude any input the Dockerfile STAGE 1 needs:
#   COPY pom.xml ./        COPY mvnw mvnw.cmd ./        COPY .mvn/ .mvn/        COPY src/ src/
# The patterns below are deliberately limited to non-inputs so the multi-stage
# build (`./mvnw clean package` then a JRE runtime) continues to succeed exactly
# as verified. In particular, the whole .mvn/ directory is intentionally NOT
# ignored (the Dockerfile copies it and `./mvnw` resolves the wrapper jar there).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Maven build output (NOT a COPY input; the fat jar is produced inside STAGE 1) ---
target/

# --- Version-control metadata (never needed inside the image) ---
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- Runtime / local log artifacts ---
*.log
logs/

# --- Local environment secrets (CWE-798: a real .env must never enter an image;
#     .env.example carries only NON-SECRET placeholders and is not a build input) ---
.env
.env.local

# --- IDE / editor metadata ---
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.vscode/
.settings/
.project
.classpath
.factorypath

# --- OS cruft ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Docker artifacts themselves (compose/Dockerfile are not build inputs of the image) ---
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore
